  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A single-page tool that runs entirely in the browser: load a batch of images, mark objects with bounding boxes or positive/negative click points, add a free-text note for each image, and export everything as one JSON file keyed by image filename. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
